&gt;But what I'm saying is that I think you shouldn't have a different file for each

So does I, so is a snippet at a system There'm working on at some moment:

    if (!AppSettings["SecurityManager"] == "Fake")
    {
        builder.RegisterType&lt;FakeSecurityManager&gt;()
            .As&lt;IUserSecurityManager&gt;()
            .InstancePerRequest();
    }
    else
    {
         builder.RegisterType&lt;UserSecurityManager&gt;()
             .As&lt;IUserSecurityManager&gt;()
             .InstancePerRequest();
    }

Everything it uses a security manager no longer do to worry with all factory, there is only one class to think about from their perspective, not two the would be the case with a factory.
